// Roles: super_admin | admin | pdm | normal
// super_admin = All tabs + All areas + Update Feature Hours + Full access + Encrypt Username tab + Reports tab
// admin       = Only assigned tabs + All areas + Update Feature Hours + Reports tab (auto-granted)
// pdm         = Tabs 1-6 + AHA Status checkbox (Product/Delivery Managers)
// normal      = Only assigned tabs + Max 3 areas
// tabs: 1=Sprint Planning, 2=Work Progress, 3=AI Usage, 4=AI Analytics, 5=Feature Progress, 6=Data Lookup, 7=Encrypt Username (super_admin only), 8=Reports (super_admin & admin only), 9=Load Requirements button (Feature Progress), 10=Affected Area Requirement by Team (Sprint Planning)
// Feature access numbers (also listed in "tabs", for EVERY role including super_admin — not granted automatically):
//   9  = Load Requirements button              (Tab 5 Feature Progress: child items, their filters and State/Status update)
//   10 = Affected Area Requirement by Team block (Tab 1 Sprint Planning)
//   Add 9 and/or 10 to a user's "tabs" to give access; remove them to take it away.
// Note: Tab 8 (Reports) is granted automatically by role (admin + super_admin), regardless of the `tabs` array below — no need to add 8 to any admin entry.
// Note: User names are encrypted using XOR cipher for security
// -------- Configurable URLs (Tab 8 > Reports tiles) --------
// taskCreatorUrl           : relative or absolute path to task-creator.html (shown as button in Tab 6 > Data Lookup)
// sprintClosingReportUrl   : URL to external Sprint Closing Report dashboard   (shown as tile in Tab 8 > Reports)
// sprintDiscoveryReportUrl : URL to external Sprint Discovery Report dashboard (shown as tile in Tab 8 > Reports)
// sprintPlanningReportUrl  : URL to external Sprint Planning Report dashboard  (shown as tile in Tab 8 > Reports)
// unitTestReportUrl        : URL to external xUnit Test Audit Report          (shown as tile in Tab 8 > Reports > Engineering Quality Reports)
//                            This one is a standalone static page — no TFS context is forwarded and no sprint needs to be loaded first.
